      "sha": "98071d401c818d61bf7992bc3c52ab19d170e928"
    },
    "body": "## What\n\nMoves the `yadgarhq/actions` hook block of `yadgarhq/store` from `v1.37.1` to `v1.38.2`. The block is regenerated from the `rust-lib` class (topic `yadgar-class-rust-lib`), as `classes.json` in `yadgarhq/actions` defines it.\n\nThe hook ids, their order and their keys already match the class, so the `rev:` line is the only change.\n\nNo other block of `.pre-commit-config.yaml` changed.\n\n## Why\n\nADR-0982: an `actions` release opens one adoption pull request per consumer, found by its class topic. ADR-0561 rules that a release fires them; ADR-0635 rules that a hook set is generated from its class. Before this, every rev bump was a hand edit and nothing detected drift.\n\nOpened by the `fan-out` workflow in `yadgarhq/actions`, as the `yadgarhq-bot` App. It proposes and never merges (ADR-0690, ADR-0531). ADR-0983: the run's report says which consumers carry `v1.38.2`.\n\n## Changelog\n\nNo release: a hook adoption changes developer tooling only, so this body carries no Conventional Commits entry and the `version` job cuts no tag for it.\n\n## Verification\n\n`ci / passed` on this pull request runs this repository's pre-commit at the new rev; that run IS the verification. Nothing was run before the pull request was opened. A repository with no CI needs `pre-commit run --all-files` on this branch before the merge.\n\nThe release range to read: https://github.com/yadgarhq/actions/compare/v1.37.1...v1.38.2\n\n## Risk\n\nMerging cuts no release of this repository. The hook block is developer tooling and is not part of what the repository ships, so the change waits for the next release a person cuts.\n\nA newer hook can red a check that passed at the old rev. That is the gate working: fix the cause in its own pull request, and never widen the gate to make it pass.\n\nA commit a person adds to this branch lands with no release, because the squash keeps the bot as author. Put such a fix in its own pull request.\n\nReversible: restore `rev: v1.37.1`. A published tag never moves, so the old rev still names the same hooks.\n\nD80: this changes developer tooling only. It renders no resource, names no cloud and no ingress implementation, and adds no trust boundary.\n",
